{"id": "0afc1748-91ec-4805-85d9-db90d70216fe", "slug": "tomorrow-intelligence-content-section", "title": "Tomorrow Intelligence Content Section", "description": "Tomorrow Intelligence Content Section is designed for structuring key content in a full-width page block. Key features include clear structure, reusable styling patterns, and production-ready layout behavior. Built with custom CSS, it is suitable for component libraries and responsive web projects. It includes animated", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-top-creators-featured\"\nname: \"Tomorrow Intelligence Content Section\"\ndescription: \"Tomorrow Intelligence Content Section is designed for structuring key content in a full-width page block. Key features include clear structure, reusable styling patterns, and production-ready layout behavior. Built with custom CSS, it is suitable for component libraries and responsive web projects. It includes animated\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#00FF64\"\n  secondary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  accent: \"#00FFC8\"\n  background: \"#E5E5E5\"\n  surface: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-primary: \"#111827\"\n  text-secondary: \"#4B5563\"\n  border: \"#E5E7EB\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Playfair Display\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"16px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Tomorrow Intelligence Content Section\nSource: Neuform Featured templates from top creators. Author: Meng To (@mengto). Views: 1; favorites: 3; remixes: 2.\nTags: background, animated, effect.\n## Overview\nTomorrow Intelligence Content Section is designed for structuring key content in a full-width page block. Key features include clear structure, reusable styling patterns, and production-ready layout behavior. Built with custom CSS, it is suitable for component libraries and responsive web projects. It includes animated\n\nExplore the future of intelligence through immersive neural network and particle animations in a sleek, minimalist interface.\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Tomorrow is calling; Intelligence is an uncharted territory.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #00FF64, secondary #FFFFFF, accent #00FFC8, background #E5E5E5, surface #FFFFFF, text-primary #111827. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Playfair Display for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Slide Deck Presentation</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500&family=Playfair+Display:wght@400;500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-[#e5e5e5] min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center p-4 md:p-8 lg:p-12 font-['Inter',sans-serif] text-white antialiased selection:bg-gray-500 selection:text-white\">\n\n    <div class=\"max-w-[1200px] w-full grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4 lg:gap-6\">\n\n        <!-- Left Panel: Data Visualization -->\n        <div class=\"relative rounded-2xl p-[1px] bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-400/60 to-gray-800/20 shadow-2xl group\">\n            <div class=\"relative bg-[#050505] rounded-[calc(1rem-1px)] h-[600px] lg:h-[750px] overflow-hidden flex flex-col\">\n\n                <!-- Canvas Container -->\n                <canvas id=\"canvas-network\" class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full z-0\"></canvas>\n\n                <!-- Content Overlay -->\n                <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-10 flex flex-col justify-end p-8 lg:p-10 pointer-events-none\">\n                    <h2 class=\"font-['Playfair_Display',serif] text-5xl lg:text-[4.5rem] tracking-tight leading-none text-gray-50 font-normal\">\n                        Tomorrow<br>is calling\n                    </h2>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Right Panel: Particle Canvas -->\n        <div class=\"relative rounded-2xl p-[1px] bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-400/60 to-gray-800/20 shadow-2xl group\">\n            <div class=\"relative bg-[#050505] rounded-[calc(1rem-1px)] h-[600px] lg:h-[750px] overflow-hidden\">\n\n                <!-- Canvas Container -->\n                <canvas id=\"canvas-particles\" class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full z-0\"></canvas>\n\n                <!-- Content Overlay -->\n                <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-10 p-8 lg:p-10 pointer-events-none\">\n                    <h2 class=\"text-3xl lg:text-[2.5rem] tracking-tight text-gray-100 leading-[1.15] font-light max-w-[85%]\">\n                        Intelligence is an<br>uncharted territory\n                    </h2>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        // --- Left Canvas: Network Flow Animation ---\n        const canvasNet = document.getElementById('canvas-network');\n        const ctxNet = canvasNet.getContext('2d');\n\n        let netW, netH;\n        let time = 0;\n\n        function resizeNet() {\n            netW = canvasNet.clientWidth;\n            netH = canvasNet.clientHeight;\n            canvasNet.width = netW * window.devicePixelRatio;\n            canvasNet.height = netH * window.devicePixelRatio;\n            ctxNet.scale(window.devicePixelRatio, window.devicePixelRatio);\n        }\n\n        window.addEventListener('resize', resizeNet);\n        resizeNet();\n\n        // Data points for curves\n        const curves = [];\n        for(let i=0; i<60; i++) {\n            curves.push({\n                angle: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\n                length: 100 + Math.random() * 200,\n                speed: 0.01 + Math.random() * 0.02,\n                offset: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\n                color: Math.random() > 0.5 ? 'rgba(0, 255, 200, 0.4)' : 'rgba(100, 150, 255, 0.4)',\n                thickness: 0.5 + Math.random() * 1.5\n            });\n        }\n\n        // Random numbers\n        const numbers = [];\n        for(let i=0; i<25; i++) {\n            numbers.push({\n                x: Math.random() * 0.8 + 0.1, // relative position\n                y: Math.random() * 0.5 + 0.1,\n                val: (Math.random() * 900 + 100).toFixed(1)\n            });\n        }\n\n        function drawNetwork() {\n            ctxNet.clearRect(0, 0, netW, netH);\n\n            // 1. Draw vertical grid\n            ctxNet.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03)';\n            ctxNet.lineWidth = 1;\n            for(let x = 0; x < netW; x += 30) {\n                ctxNet.beginPath();\n                ctxNet.moveTo(x, 0);\n                ctxNet.lineTo(x, netH);\n                ctxNet.stroke();\n            }\n\n            const centerX = netW * 0.45;\n            const centerY = netH * 0.35;\n            const boxW = 280;\n            const boxH = 320;\n            const boxX = centerX - boxW/2;\n            const boxY = centerY - boxH/2;\n\n            // 2. Draw glowing curves\n            ctxNet.globalCompositeOperation = 'screen';\n            curves.forEach((c, i) => {\n                const currentAngle = c.angle + Math.sin(time * c.speed + c.offset) * 0.2;\n                const endX = centerX + Math.cos(currentAngle) * c.length;\n                const endY = centerY + Math.sin(currentAngle) * c.length;\n\n                // Control point for bezier\n                const cpX = centerX + Math.cos(currentAngle - 0.5) * (c.length * 0.5);\n                const cpY = centerY + Math.sin(currentAngle - 0.5) * (c.length * 0.5);\n\n                ctxNet.beginPath();\n                ctxNet.moveTo(centerX, centerY);\n                ctxNet.quadraticCurveTo(cpX, cpY, endX, endY);\n\n                ctxNet.strokeStyle = c.color;\n                ctxNet.lineWidth = c.thickness;\n                ctxNet.stroke();\n\n                // Draw small dots at ends occasionally\n                if(Math.sin(time * c.speed * 5 + i) > 0.8) {\n                    ctxNet.beginPath();\n                    ctxNet.arc(endX, endY, 1.5, 0, Math.PI*2);\n                    ctxNet.fillStyle = '#fff';\n                    ctxNet.fill();\n                }\n            });\n            ctxNet.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';\n\n            // 3. Draw bounding box (Green)\n            ctxNet.strokeStyle = 'rgba(0, 255, 100, 0.5)';\n            ctxNet.lineWidth = 1;\n            ctxNet.strokeRect(boxX, boxY, boxW, boxH);\n\n            // 4. Draw bottom perspective lines & label\n            const labelY = boxY + boxH + 120;\n            const labelW = 80;\n            const labelH = 24;\n            const labelX = centerX - labelW/2;\n\n            // Lines connecting box corners to label\n            ctxNet.strokeStyle = 'rgba(150, 100, 255, 0.4)';\n            ctxNet.beginPath();\n            ctxNet.moveTo(boxX, boxY + boxH); // Bottom left\n            ctxNet.lineTo(labelX, labelY);\n            ctxNet.moveTo(boxX + boxW, boxY + boxH); // Bottom right\n            ctxNet.lineTo(labelX + labelW, labelY);\n\n            // Cross lines\n            ctxNet.moveTo(boxX, boxY + boxH);\n            ctxNet.lineTo(labelX + labelW, labelY);\n            ctxNet.moveTo(boxX + boxW, boxY + boxH);\n            ctxNet.lineTo(labelX, labelY);\n\n            ctxNet.stroke();\n\n            // Additional white perspective lines\n            ctxNet.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2)';\n            ctxNet.beginPath();\n            ctxNet.moveTo(boxX + boxW/2, boxY + boxH);\n            ctxNet.lineTo(labelX + labelW/2, labelY);\n            ctxNet.stroke();\n\n            // Label Box\n            ctxNet.strokeStyle = 'rgba(0, 255, 100, 0.6)';\n            ctxNet.strokeRect(labelX, labelY, labelW, labelH);\n            ctxNet.fillStyle = 'rgba(0, 255, 100, 0.8)';\n            ctxNet.font = '10px Inter';\n            ctxNet.textAlign = 'center';\n            ctxNet.textBaseline = 'middle';\n            ctxNet.fillText('NeuralNet', labelX + labelW/2, labelY + labelH/2);\n\n            // 5. Draw scattered numbers\n            ctxNet.fillStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7)';\n            ctxNet.font = '9px Inter';\n            ctxNet.textAlign = 'left';\n            numbers.forEach(n => {\n                const nx = boxX + n.x * boxW;\n                const ny = boxY + n.y * boxH;\n                // Add slight floating motion\n                const floatY = ny + Math.sin(time + n.x * 10) * 2;\n                ctxNet.fillText(n.val, nx, floatY);\n                // Draw tiny dot next to number\n                ctxNet.beginPath();\n                ctxNet.arc(nx - 4, floatY, 0.8, 0, Math.PI*2);\n                ctxNet.fill();\n            });\n\n            time += 0.05;\n            requestAnimationFrame(drawNetwork);\n        }\n        drawNetwork();\n\n\n        // --- Right Canvas: Particle Swarm Animation ---\n        const canvasPart = document.getElementById('canvas-particles');\n        const ctxPart = canvasPart.getContext('2d');\n\n        let partW, partH;\n\n        function resizePart() {\n            partW = canvasPart.clientWidth;\n            partH = canvasPart.clientHeight;\n            canvasPart.width = partW * window.devicePixelRatio;\n            canvasPart.height = partH * window.devicePixelRatio;\n            ctxPart.scale(window.devicePixelRatio, window.devicePixelRatio);\n        }\n\n        window.addEventListener('resize', resizePart);\n        resizePart();\n\n        const particles = [];\n        const colors = ['#f97316', '#eab308', '#06b6d4', '#ef4444', '#10b981']; // Tailwind orange, yellow, cyan, red, emerald\n\n        for(let i=0; i<150; i++) {\n            particles.push({\n                x: Math.random() * partW,\n                y: Math.random() * partH,\n                vx: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.3,\n                vy: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.3 - 0.2, // slight upward drift\n                radius: Math.random() * 1.5 + 0.5,\n                color: colors[Math.floor(Math.random() * colors.length)],\n                alpha: Math.random() * 0.5 + 0.3\n            });\n        }\n\n        function drawParticles() {\n            ctxPart.clearRect(0, 0, partW, partH);\n\n            particles.forEach(p => {\n                p.x += p.vx;\n                p.y += p.vy;\n\n                // Wrap around\n                if(p.y < -10) p.y = partH + 10;\n                if(p.x < -10) p.x = partW + 10;\n                if(p.x > partW + 10) p.x = -10;\n\n                ctxPart.beginPath();\n                ctxPart.arc(p.x, p.y, p.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n                ctxPart.fillStyle = p.color;\n                ctxPart.globalAlpha = p.alpha;\n                ctxPart.fill();\n            });\n\n            ctxPart.globalAlpha = 1; // reset\n\n            requestAnimationFrame(drawParticles);\n        }\n        drawParticles();\n\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "tomorrow-intelligence-content-section.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/regenerated-2026-05-22-2s/tomorrow-intelligence-content-section.jpg", "source_name": "tomorrow-intelligence-content-section-DESIGN.md", "views": 69, "forks": 4, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "9109ecbb-cdc4-4815-981e-2ea83be13765", "created_at": "2026-05-01T16:18:09.070118+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-06-29T12:11:27.360135+00:00"}